{"timestamp":"2026-09-29T11:20:36.661Z","level":"info","event":"provider.together.response","fields":{"provider":"together","endpoint":"/chat/completions","response":{"httpStatus":200,"contentType":"text/event-stream","providerRequestId":"b4ff9aa2-aws_ec1","model":"moonshotai/Kimi-K3","text":"{\n  \"schemaVersion\": \"objectives-v2\",\n  \"objectives\": [\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"Describe trimester-appropriate movement strategies for pregnancy, including a 10-minute walk in the first trimester, gradual progression with the talk test in the second, and shorter, lower-intensity sessions in the third, and explain how gentle activity supports circulation, blood sugar regulation, and labor endurance.\",\n      \"verb\": \"describe\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"ab1cf706-71bd-7ca1-b531-ab624c44f3e1\", \"fa06903c-8540-7e50-9188-568c594b21ce\", \"9e81e435-fab4-764f-83d3-5204b40898b5\", \"2b77cfe1-1bdd-7008-8cf4-8139f72a6b92\", \"d9307a6f-83b3-716c-bdaf-ff3eb467b91e\"],\n      \"confidence\": 0.95\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"Explain how eating protein at every meal and taking prenatal vitamins at night with food support pregnancy wellbeing, identifying suitable protein foods, relevant safety guidelines, and why evening dosing with food can reduce iron-related nausea.\",\n      \"verb\": \"explain\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"43f06ae2-beb0-703b-89e0-7ce9ac8db8fd\", \"0cb42f00-59f9-736f-8af7-4406fbd9902c\", \"b31413e5-3aaf-7fde-8e77-930eb14e08f6\", \"5621d9a6-35b9-7bd5-a9bd-bf90b893abeb\", \"ba4d898c-1f1d-702e-b84f-bf26e5401922\", \"59033b68-f011-7e5d-8f35-aa1bc2fb5832\", \"a403f9c5-23eb-73d2-8e9d-8d6cdb785e21\"],\n      \"confidence\": 0.93\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"Identify the urgent red-flag symptoms that require immediate reporting during pregnancy, and apply a plan for managing health worries that replaces late-night symptom searching and crowdsourced opinions with trusted sources and prompt contact with the care team.\",\n      \"verb\": \"identify\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"f245f1d0-3b10-75ee-8a6d-1e186f8b7b22\", \"4b304eb9-058a-7626-9c81-bbdaa02a61b8\", \"55308f25-9a85-7a2f-ba86-82f8e5de2cf7\", \"cbc62292-71de-78eb-93e1-cf5532bf947d\", \"d545a14b-3707-74bf-b162-86263bd568ae\", \"b73821e8-2cc4-7e89-aed7-cdfc16f2ef61\"],\n      \"confidence\": 0.94\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"Explain how learning about labo","textChunks":["{\n  \"schemaVersion\": \"objectives-v2\",\n  \"objectives\": [\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"Describe trimester-appropriate movement strategies for pregnancy, including a 10-minute walk in the first trimester, gradual progression with the talk test in the second, and shorter, lower-intensity sessions in the third, and explain how gentle activity supports circulation, blood sugar regulation, and labor endurance.\",\n      \"verb\": \"describe\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"ab1cf706-71bd-7ca1-b531-ab624c44f3e1\", \"fa06903c-8540-7e50-9188-568c594b21ce\", \"9e81e435-fab4-764f-83d3-5204b40898b5\", \"2b77cfe1-1bdd-7008-8cf4-8139f72a6b92\", \"d9307a6f-83b3-716c-bdaf-ff3eb467b91e\"],\n      \"confidence\": 0.95\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"Explain how eating protein at every meal and taking prenatal vitamins at night with food support pregnancy wellbeing, identifying suitable protein foods, relevant safety guidelines, and why evening dosing with food can reduce iron-related nausea.\",\n      \"verb\": \"explain\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"43f06ae2-beb0-703b-89e0-7ce9ac8db8fd\", \"0cb42f00-59f9-736f-8af7-4406fbd9902c\", \"b31413e5-3aaf-7fde-8e77-930eb14e08f6\", \"5621d9a6-35b9-7bd5-a9bd-bf90b893abeb\", \"ba4d898c-1f1d-702e-b84f-bf26e5401922\", \"59033b68-f011-7e5d-8f35-aa1bc2fb5832\", \"a403f9c5-23eb-73d2-8e9d-8d6cdb785e21\"],\n      \"confidence\": 0.93\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"Identify the urgent red-flag symptoms that require immediate reporting during pregnancy, and apply a plan for managing health worries that replaces late-night symptom searching and crowdsourced opinions with trusted sources and prompt contact with the care team.\",\n      \"verb\": \"identify\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"f245f1d0-3b10-75ee-8a6d-1e186f8b7b22\", \"4b304eb9-058a-7626-9c81-bbdaa02a61b8\", \"55308f25-9a85-7a2f-ba86-82f8e5de2cf7\", \"cbc62292-71de-78eb-93e1-cf5532bf947d\", \"d545a14b-3707-74bf-b162-86263bd568ae\", \"b73821e8-2cc4-7e89-aed7-cdfc16f2ef61\"],\n      \"confidence\": 0.94\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"Explain how learning about labo","r stages, contractions, and normal progression, together with training the pelvic floor for both strength and relaxation, can reduce fear and help a woman participate actively in birth.\",\n      \"verb\": \"explain\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"97f28d00-1622-7b1b-97c1-75effbb4a461\", \"02fa95aa-3ed8-7dd9-90ce-5e6fc65d2c48\", \"6a171c18-28c8-7559-b82b-7a6ad772ad05\", \"a41862a7-efdf-7f3f-b46e-518eecb9affa\", \"30c28461-607e-745c-b1bb-0ba6b3963b9c\"],\n      \"confidence\": 0.92\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"Describe how journaling preserves emotions, fears, questions, and milestones that photos cannot capture, and outline a weekly postpartum planning routine that addresses the mother's recovery, sleep disruption, hormonal changes, meals, practical help, and emotional support.\",\n      \"verb\": \"describe\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"b91f499f-4809-7274-9b35-db1432456f86\", \"dce93289-fc2d-701c-9c11-0961fb3a114f\", \"4e76ff18-b457-7a52-8126-7f7a5118b61a\", \"1a5ed54b-8c0a-7bb8-89fe-ee8da33d8070\"],\n      \"confidence\": 0.92\n    }\n  ],\n  \"keyConcepts\": [\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Trimester-appropriate physical activity\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"ab1cf706-71bd-7ca1-b531-ab624c44f3e1\", \"fa06903c-8540-7e50-9188-568c594b21ce\", \"9e81e435-fab4-764f-83d3-5204b40898b5\", \"2b77cfe1-1bdd-7008-8cf4-8139f72a6b92\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Protein intake and food safety in pregnancy\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"43f06ae2-beb0-703b-89e0-7ce9ac8db8fd\", \"0cb42f00-59f9-736f-8af7-4406fbd9902c\", \"b31413e5-3aaf-7fde-8e77-930eb14e08f6\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Prenatal vitamin timing and tolerability\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"ba4d898c-1f1d-702e-b84f-bf26e5401922\", \"59033b68-f011-7e5d-8f35-aa1bc2fb5832\", \"a403f9c5-23eb-73d2-8e9d-8d6cdb785e21\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Red-flag symptoms and reliable information sources\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"f245f1d0-3b10-75ee-8a6d-1e186f8b7b22\", \"4b304eb9-058a-7626-9c81-bbdaa02a61b8\", \"cbc62292-71de-78eb-93e1-cf5532bf947d\", \"b73821e8-2cc4-7e89-aed7-cdfc16f2ef61\"]\n    },\n    ","{\n      \"text\": \"Labor preparation and pelvic floor training\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"97f28d00-1622-7b1b-97c1-75effbb4a461\", \"02fa95aa-3ed8-7dd9-90ce-5e6fc65d2c48\", \"6a171c18-28c8-7559-b82b-7a6ad772ad05\", \"a41862a7-efdf-7f3f-b46e-518eecb9affa\", \"30c28461-607e-745c-b1bb-0ba6b3963b9c\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Journaling and postpartum planning\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"b91f499f-4809-7274-9b35-db1432456f86\", \"dce93289-fc2d-701c-9c11-0961fb3a114f\", \"4e76ff18-b457-7a52-8126-7f7a5118b61a\", \"1a5ed54b-8c0a-7bb8-89fe-ee8da33d8070\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prerequisiteKnowledge\": [\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Basic familiarity with the three trimesters of pregnancy and that physical and energy changes occur across them.\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"fa06903c-8540-7e50-9188-568c594b21ce\", \"9e81e435-fab4-764f-83d3-5204b40898b5\", \"2b77cfe1-1bdd-7008-8cf4-8139f72a6b92\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"General awareness that pregnancy involves hormonal changes affecting digestion, appetite, and blood sugar.\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"43f06ae2-beb0-703b-89e0-7ce9ac8db8fd\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Knowing that prenatal vitamins are commonly recommended in pregnancy and often contain iron.\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"ba4d898c-1f1d-702e-b84f-bf26e5401922\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Basic understanding that labor is physically demanding and involves contractions and stages.\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"ab1cf706-71bd-7ca1-b531-ab624c44f3e1\", \"97f28d00-1622-7b1b-97c1-75effbb4a461\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"vocabulary\": [\n    {\n      \"term\": \"Talk test\",\n      \"definition\": \"A way to gauge exercise intensity: if you are too winded to speak a full sentence, reduce the intensity.\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"9e81e435-fab4-764f-83d3-5204b40898b5\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"term\": \"Amino acids\",\n      \"definition\": \"Building blocks supplied by protein that are needed for growth and development during pregnancy.\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"43f06ae2-beb0-703b-89e0-7ce9ac8db8fd\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"term\": \"Red flags\",\n ","     \"definition\": \"Urgent warning signs in pregnancy - such as heavy bleeding, severe abdominal pain, chest pain, difficulty breathing, sudden swelling, or decreased fetal movement - that should be reported immediately.\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"f245f1d0-3b10-75ee-8a6d-1e186f8b7b22\", \"4b304eb9-058a-7626-9c81-bbdaa02a61b8\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"term\": \"Transition\",\n      \"definition\": \"A phase of labor that can feel intense; knowing what it feels like can make contractions easier to interpret.\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"02fa95aa-3ed8-7dd9-90ce-5e6fc65d2c48\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"term\": \"Pelvic floor\",\n      \"definition\": \"The group of muscles that supports the uterus, bladder, and bowel and needs both strength and the ability to relax during birth.\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"6a171c18-28c8-7559-b82b-7a6ad772ad05\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"term\": \"Pelvic floor physical therapist\",\n      \"definition\": \"A specialist who can assess the pelvic floor during pregnancy and guide exercises that include both engagement and relaxation.\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"30c28461-607e-745c-b1bb-0ba6b3963b9c\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"misconceptions\": [\n    {\n      \"misconception\": \"Exercise should be avoided during pregnancy, especially when you feel unwell.\",\n      \"correction\": \"Gentle, gradual movement such as a 10-minute walk can support circulation and blood sugar regulation and may help with nausea, though a medical provider should always be consulted before starting or changing an exercise program.\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"fa06903c-8540-7e50-9188-568c594b21ce\", \"ab1cf706-71bd-7ca1-b531-ab624c44f3e1\", \"d9307a6f-83b3-716c-bdaf-ff3eb467b91e\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"misconception\": \"Prenatal vitamins must be taken in the morning on an empty stomach.\",\n      \"correction\": \"Because iron in prenatals may cause nausea, taking them with dinner or at bedtime may make them easier to tolerate, and vitamin C-containing foods can support iron absorption.\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"ba4d898c-1f1d-702e-b84f-","bf26e5401922\", \"59033b68-f011-7e5d-8f35-aa1bc2fb5832\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"misconception\": \"Searching symptoms online at night is a reliable way to assess pregnancy concerns.\",\n      \"correction\": \"Late-night searching can increase anxiety because results emphasize serious but uncommon conditions; it is better to use trusted sources and contact the care team for concerning symptoms.\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"55308f25-9a85-7a2f-ba86-82f8e5de2cf7\", \"cbc62292-71de-78eb-93e1-cf5532bf947d\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"misconception\": \"Pelvic floor training means only doing Kegel squeezes.\",\n      \"correction\": \"Pelvic floor exercises are not only about squeezing; for some people excessive tightening can worsen an already overactive or tight pelvic floor, so training should include both engagement and relaxation.\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"a41862a7-efdf-7f3f-b46e-518eecb9affa\", \"30c28461-607e-745c-b1bb-0ba6b3963b9c\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"misconception\": \"Preparing for a baby mainly means buying baby supplies.\",\n      \"correction\": \"Preparation should also include the mother's recovery, sleep disruption, hormonal changes, meals, practical help, and emotional support.\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"4e76ff18-b457-7a52-8126-7f7a5118b61a\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"assessmentQuestions\": [\n    {\n      \"question\": \"What is a suggested first-trimester activity, and what two benefits does the source say gentle movement can support?\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"fa06903c-8540-7e50-9188-568c594b21ce\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"question\": \"Explain how the \\\"talk test\\\" helps a pregnant woman adjust her exercise intensity in the second trimester.\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"9e81e435-fab4-764f-83d3-5204b40898b5\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"question\": \"Why might taking a prenatal vitamin with dinner or at bedtime be easier to tolerate than taking it on an empty stomach?\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"ba4d898c-1f1d-702e-b84f-bf26e5401922\", \"59033b68-f011-7e5d-8f35-aa1bc2fb5832\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"question\": \"List at least f","our red-flag symptoms that should be reported immediately during pregnancy.\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"f245f1d0-3b10-75ee-8a6d-1e186f8b7b22\", \"4b304eb9-058a-7626-9c81-bbdaa02a61b8\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"question\": \"Why does the source recommend training the pelvic floor for relaxation as well as strength?\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"6a171c18-28c8-7559-b82b-7a6ad772ad05\", \"a41862a7-efdf-7f3f-b46e-518eecb9affa\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"question\": \"Give two examples of weekly postpartum planning tasks suggested in the source and explain why they go beyond buying baby supplies.\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"1a5ed54b-8c0a-7bb8-89fe-ee8da33d8070\", \"4e76ff18-b457-7a52-8126-7f7a5118b61a\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"focusCoverage\": {\n    \"status\": \"covered\"\n  }\n}"],"textChunksTruncated":false,"textCharacters":10745,"reasoningCharacters":0,"finishReason":"stop","inputTokens":"[REDACTED]","outputTokens":"[REDACTED]"},"retries":0,"latencyMs":54402,"service":"pipeline-worker","correlationId":"01a0ece2-fd2f-7533-9408-bed00830d7cb"}}
