{"timestamp":"2026-09-29T11:21:09.697Z","level":"info","event":"provider.together.response","fields":{"provider":"together","endpoint":"/chat/completions","response":{"httpStatus":200,"contentType":"text/event-stream","providerRequestId":"36527189-aws_ec1","model":"moonshotai/Kimi-K3","text":"{\n  \"schemaVersion\": \"outline-v1\",\n  \"targetDurationSeconds\": 300,\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"hook\",\n      \"title\": \"Pregnancy without the 2 a.m. panic\",\n      \"description\": \"Frame the lesson around the focus: small, concrete habits that protect both health and sanity during pregnancy. Promise a clear flow from daily routines (movement, food, vitamins) to mental calm (journaling, trusted information) to big-picture preparation (labor knowledge, pelvic floor, postpartum planning).\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\n        \"01a0ece3-d352-7b69-aa7c-51c56ee5fd19\",\n        \"01a0ece3-d352-718d-96e7-e965f1985968\",\n        \"01a0ece3-d352-782b-9060-cd87a477fe55\",\n        \"01a0ece3-d352-75c7-a3bc-209c0cc9ae4e\",\n        \"01a0ece3-d352-781e-871c-1d262e9f9ccc\"\n      ],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 25,\n      \"framingNote\": \"Generated framing device that sets up the lesson flow and tone; it introduces no factual claims beyond the approved objectives.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"concept\",\n      \"title\": \"Move by trimester: a pattern that changes with you\",\n      \"description\": \"Teach the trimester-by-trimester movement pattern: a 10-minute walk in the first trimester, gradual progression using the talk test in the second, and shorter, lower-intensity sessions in the third. Explain why gentle activity matters for circulation, blood sugar regulation, endurance for labor, and recovery, and note the safety step of consulting a provider before changing exercise.\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\n        \"01a0ece3-d352-7b69-aa7c-51c56ee5fd19\"\n      ],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\n        \"ab1cf706-71bd-7ca1-b531-ab624c44f3e1\",\n        \"fa06903c-8540-7e50-9188-568c594b21ce\",\n        \"9e81e435-fab4-764f-83d3-5204b40898b5\",\n        \"2b77cfe1-1bdd-7008-8cf4-8139f72a6b92\",\n        \"d9307a6f-83b3-716c-bdaf-ff3eb467b91e\"\n      ],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 45\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"concept\",\n      \"title\": \"Fuel and vitamins: protein at every meal, prenatals at night\",\n      ","textChunks":["{\n  \"schemaVersion\": \"outline-v1\",\n  \"targetDurationSeconds\": 300,\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"hook\",\n      \"title\": \"Pregnancy without the 2 a.m. panic\",\n      \"description\": \"Frame the lesson around the focus: small, concrete habits that protect both health and sanity during pregnancy. Promise a clear flow from daily routines (movement, food, vitamins) to mental calm (journaling, trusted information) to big-picture preparation (labor knowledge, pelvic floor, postpartum planning).\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\n        \"01a0ece3-d352-7b69-aa7c-51c56ee5fd19\",\n        \"01a0ece3-d352-718d-96e7-e965f1985968\",\n        \"01a0ece3-d352-782b-9060-cd87a477fe55\",\n        \"01a0ece3-d352-75c7-a3bc-209c0cc9ae4e\",\n        \"01a0ece3-d352-781e-871c-1d262e9f9ccc\"\n      ],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 25,\n      \"framingNote\": \"Generated framing device that sets up the lesson flow and tone; it introduces no factual claims beyond the approved objectives.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"concept\",\n      \"title\": \"Move by trimester: a pattern that changes with you\",\n      \"description\": \"Teach the trimester-by-trimester movement pattern: a 10-minute walk in the first trimester, gradual progression using the talk test in the second, and shorter, lower-intensity sessions in the third. Explain why gentle activity matters for circulation, blood sugar regulation, endurance for labor, and recovery, and note the safety step of consulting a provider before changing exercise.\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\n        \"01a0ece3-d352-7b69-aa7c-51c56ee5fd19\"\n      ],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\n        \"ab1cf706-71bd-7ca1-b531-ab624c44f3e1\",\n        \"fa06903c-8540-7e50-9188-568c594b21ce\",\n        \"9e81e435-fab4-764f-83d3-5204b40898b5\",\n        \"2b77cfe1-1bdd-7008-8cf4-8139f72a6b92\",\n        \"d9307a6f-83b3-716c-bdaf-ff3eb467b91e\"\n      ],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 45\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"concept\",\n      \"title\": \"Fuel and vitamins: protein at every meal, prenatals at night\",\n      ","\"description\": \"Explain the two-part nutrition habit: include protein at every meal to make meals more filling and supply amino acids for growth and development, and take prenatal vitamins with dinner or at bedtime to reduce iron-related nausea. List suitable protein foods, flag the safety guidelines (avoid high-mercury and raw or undercooked fish, handle deli meats per guidance), and share the nightstand snack and habit-placement tips.\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\n        \"01a0ece3-d352-718d-96e7-e965f1985968\"\n      ],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\n        \"43f06ae2-beb0-703b-89e0-7ce9ac8db8fd\",\n        \"0cb42f00-59f9-736f-8af7-4406fbd9902c\",\n        \"b31413e5-3aaf-7fde-8e77-930eb14e08f6\",\n        \"5621d9a6-35b9-7bd5-a9bd-bf90b893abeb\",\n        \"ba4d898c-1f1d-702e-b84f-bf26e5401922\",\n        \"59033b68-f011-7e5d-8f35-aa1bc2fb5832\",\n        \"a403f9c5-23eb-73d2-8e9d-8d6cdb785e21\"\n      ],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 50\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"concept\",\n      \"title\": \"Calm the worry loop: red flags, trusted sources, no 2 a.m. Googling\",\n      \"description\": \"Walk through the information-anxiety flow: why late-night symptom searching and crowdsourced opinions increase anxiety, the action plan of setting an evening cutoff and bookmarking trusted sources, the urgent red-flag symptoms that require immediate reporting (heavy bleeding, severe abdominal pain, headache, vision changes, chest pain, difficulty breathing, sudden swelling of face or hands, leaking fluid, decreased fetal movement, thoughts of self-harm), and the strategy of relying on one trusted clinician plus one evidence-based source.\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\n        \"01a0ece3-d352-782b-9060-cd87a477fe55\"\n      ],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\n        \"55308f25-9a85-7a2f-ba86-82f8e5de2cf7\",\n        \"cbc62292-71de-78eb-93e1-cf5532bf947d\",\n        \"f245f1d0-3b10-75ee-8a6d-1e186f8b7b22\",\n        \"4b304eb9-058a-7626-9c81-bbdaa02a61b8\",\n        \"d545a14b-3707-74bf-b162-86263bd568ae\",\n        \"b73821e8-2cc4-7e89-aed7-cdfc16f","2ef61\"\n      ],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 55\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"concept\",\n      \"title\": \"Know labor, train your pelvic floor: from passenger to participant\",\n      \"description\": \"Show how understanding labor stages, contractions, and normal progression (including what transition can feel like) reduces fear and helps a woman work with her body. Then explain pelvic floor training: these muscles support the uterus, bladder, and bowel and need both strength and relaxation for birth; squeezing alone is not the whole picture, and a pelvic floor physical therapist or an evidence-based program covering engagement and relaxation can help.\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\n        \"01a0ece3-d352-75c7-a3bc-209c0cc9ae4e\"\n      ],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\n        \"97f28d00-1622-7b1b-97c1-75effbb4a461\",\n        \"02fa95aa-3ed8-7dd9-90ce-5e6fc65d2c48\",\n        \"6a171c18-28c8-7559-b82b-7a6ad772ad05\",\n        \"a41862a7-efdf-7f3f-b46e-518eecb9affa\",\n        \"30c28461-607e-745c-b1bb-0ba6b3963b9c\"\n      ],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 45\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"concept\",\n      \"title\": \"Write it down, plan ahead: journaling and weekly postpartum prep\",\n      \"description\": \"Explain how journaling preserves what photos cannot: emotions, fears, excitement, questions, and milestones like first feeling the baby move. Then outline the weekly postpartum planning routine: one manageable task per week covering the mother's recovery, sleep disruption, hormonal changes, meals, practical help, and emotional support, such as drafting a meal plan or identifying a trusted person to call on hard days.\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\n        \"01a0ece3-d352-781e-871c-1d262e9f9ccc\"\n      ],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\n        \"b91f499f-4809-7274-9b35-db1432456f86\",\n        \"dce93289-fc2d-701c-9c11-0961fb3a114f\",\n        \"4e76ff18-b457-7a52-8126-7f7a5118b61a\",\n        \"1a5ed54b-8c0a-7bb8-89fe-ee8da33d8070\"\n      ],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 45\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"summary\",\n      \"title\": \"Your ten-ha","bit flow, from today to birth and beyond\",\n      \"description\": \"Recap the whole pattern: trimester-matched movement, protein at every meal with prenatals at night, a calm information plan with red flags memorized and trusted sources bookmarked, labor knowledge plus pelvic floor training for active participation, and journaling with weekly postpartum planning. Close by encouraging learners to pick one habit to start this week.\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\n        \"01a0ece3-d352-7b69-aa7c-51c56ee5fd19\",\n        \"01a0ece3-d352-718d-96e7-e965f1985968\",\n        \"01a0ece3-d352-782b-9060-cd87a477fe55\",\n        \"01a0ece3-d352-75c7-a3bc-209c0cc9ae4e\",\n        \"01a0ece3-d352-781e-871c-1d262e9f9ccc\"\n      ],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\n        \"fa06903c-8540-7e50-9188-568c594b21ce\",\n        \"43f06ae2-beb0-703b-89e0-7ce9ac8db8fd\",\n        \"59033b68-f011-7e5d-8f35-aa1bc2fb5832\",\n        \"4b304eb9-058a-7626-9c81-bbdaa02a61b8\",\n        \"b73821e8-2cc4-7e89-aed7-cdfc16f2ef61\",\n        \"97f28d00-1622-7b1b-97c1-75effbb4a461\",\n        \"6a171c18-28c8-7559-b82b-7a6ad772ad05\",\n        \"b91f499f-4809-7274-9b35-db1432456f86\",\n        \"1a5ed54b-8c0a-7bb8-89fe-ee8da33d8070\"\n      ],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 35\n