736f-8af7-4406fbd9902c\",\n        \"b31413e5-3aaf-7fde-8e77-930eb14e08f6\",\n        \"5621d9a6-35b9-7bd5-a9bd-bf90b893abeb\",\n        \"ba4d898c-1f1d-702e-b84f-bf26e5401922\",\n        \"59033b68-f011-7e5d-8f35-aa1bc2fb5832\",\n        \"a403f9c5-23eb-73d2-8e9d-8d6cdb785e21\"\n      ],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 45\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"concept\",\n      \"title\": \"Calm the worry loop: red flags, trusted sources, no 2 a.m. Googling\",\n      \"description\": \"Walk through the information-anxiety flow: why late-night symptom searching and crowdsourced opinions increase anxiety, the action plan of setting an evening cu","toff and bookmarking trusted sources, the urgent red-flag symptoms that require immediate reporting (heavy bleeding, severe abdominal pain, headache, vision changes, chest pain, difficulty breathing, sudden swelling of face or hands, leaking fluid, decreased fetal movement, thoughts of self-harm), and the strategy of relying on one trusted clinician plus one evidence-based source.\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\n        \"01a0ece3-d352-782b-9060-cd87a477fe55\"\n      ],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\n        \"55308f25-9a85-7a2f-ba86-82f8e5de2cf7\",\n        \"cbc62292-71de-78eb-93e1-cf5532bf947d\",\n        \"f245f1d0-3b10-75ee-8a6d-1e186f8b7b22\",\n        \"4b304eb9-058a-7626-9c81-bbdaa02a61b8\",\n        \"d545a14b-3707-74bf-b162-86263bd568ae\",\n        \"b73821e8-2cc4-7e89-aed7-cdfc16f2ef61\"\n      ],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 50\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"concept\",\n      \"title\": \"Know labor, train your pelvic floor: from passenger to participant\",\n      \"description\": \"Show how understanding labor stages, contractions, and normal progression (including what transition can feel like) reduces fear and helps a woman work with her body. Then explain pelvic floor training: these muscles support the uterus, bladder, and bowel and need both strength and relaxation for birth; squeezing alone is not the whole picture, and a pelvic floor physical therapist or an evidence-based program covering engagement and relaxation can help.\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\n        \"01a0ece3-d352-75c7-a3bc-209c0cc9ae4e\"\n      ],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\n        \"97f28d00-1622-7b1b-97c1-75effbb4a461\",\n        \"02fa95aa-3ed8-7dd9-90ce-5e6fc65d2c48\",\n        \"6a171c18-28c8-7559-b82b-7a6ad772ad05\",\n        \"a41862a7-efdf-7f3f-b46e-518eecb9affa\",\n        \"30c28461-607e-745c-b1bb-0ba6b3963b9c\"\n      ],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 40\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"concept\",\n      \"title\": \"Write it down, plan ahead: journaling and weekly postpartum prep\",\n      \"description\": \"Explain how journaling preserves what photos cannot",": emotions, fears, excitement, questions, and milestones like first feeling the baby move. Then outline the weekly postpartum planning routine: one manageable task per week covering the mother's recovery, sleep disruption, hormonal changes, meals, practical help, and emotional support, such as drafting a meal plan or identifying a trusted person to call on hard days.\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\n        \"01a0ece3-d352-781e-871c-1d262e9f9ccc\"\n      ],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\n        \"b91f499f-4809-7274-9b35-db1432456f86\",\n        \"dce93289-fc2d-701c-9c11-0961fb3a114f\",\n        \"4e76ff18-b457-7a52-8126-7f7a5118b61a\",\n        \"1a5ed54b-8c0a-7bb8-89fe-ee8da33d8070\"\n      ],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 45\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"summary\",\n      \"title\": \"Your ten-habit flow, from today to birth and beyond\",\n      \"description\": \"Recap the whole pattern: trimester-matched movement, protein at every meal with prenatals at night, a calm information plan with red flags memorized and trusted sources bookmarked, labor knowledge plus pelvic floor training for active participation, and journaling with weekly postpartum planning. Close by encouraging learners to pick one habit to start this week.\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\n        \"01a0ece3-d352-7b69-aa7c-51c56ee5fd19\",\n        \"01a0ece3-d352-718d-96e7-e965f1985968\",\n        \"01a0ece3-d352-782b-9060-cd87a477fe55\",\n        \"01a0ece3-d352-75c7-a3bc-209c0cc9ae4e\",\n        \"01a0ece3-d352-781e-871c-1d262e9f9ccc\"\n      ],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\n        \"fa06903c-8540-7e50-9188-568c594b21ce\",\n        \"43f06ae2-beb0-703b-89e0-7ce9ac8db8fd\",\n        \"59033b68-f011-7e5d-8f35-aa1bc2fb5832\",\n        \"4b304eb9-058a-7626-9c81-bbdaa02a61b8\",\n        \"b73821e8-2cc4-7e89-aed7-cdfc16f2ef61\",\n        \"97f28d00-1622-7b1b-97c1-75effbb4a461\",\n        \"6a171c18-28c8-7559-b82b-7a6ad772ad05\",\n        \"b91f499f-4809-7274-9b35-db1432456f86\",\n        \"1a5ed54b-8c0a-7bb8-89fe-ee8da33d8070\"\n      ],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 35\n    }\n  ]\n}"],"textChunksTruncated":false,"textCharacters":7983,"reasoningCharacters":0,"finishReason":"stop","inputTokens":"[REDACTED]","outputTokens":"[REDACTED]"},"retries":0,"latencyMs":25338,"service":"pipeline-worker","correlationId":"01a0ece2-fd2f-7533-9408-bed00830d7cb"}}
